note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note gpu/nvidia/checks/arest.om: the shared part of the arest-* checks, the launch(), cache() and steps() blocks of
note CUDApp tests/api_rest_diff.c. Each apirest unit carries om2 and is a program's head alone, so each has its own
note check: the unit's parts (gpu/units.tsv), lib.om, lib-om2.om, its arest-UNIT.om (text t_name, text t_au, fn
note arop) and then this part. Rows:
note   UNIT NY Q E R
note Q is the call's input words (16 hex digits each, - for none), which arop gives the unit in its own layout; NY
note is the length of the unit's output view. E lists (index, value) word pairs, 16 hex digits each, that the
note outputs must hold: index i below 64 is output word i, index 64 + j is word j of an edited q after the call. R
note is the unit's answer, one word of 16 hex digits; it is last so that the gate's table control changes a word.
note The rows hold at most 64 input words and 64 output words, the largest of the calls.
fn cname to void
for i ulong len t_name bound 64
ckoc ulong get t_name i
end
end
note word j of field i, a run of 16 hex digits
fn arw i ulong j ulong to ulong
w = ulong 0
for k ulong 8
w = or shl w 8 ckhex i add mul j 8 k
end
ret w
end
fn crow to bool
if or ne ckcnt 5 not ckis 0 t_au
ckbad
end
ny = cknum 1
nb = ckhexn 2
eb = ckhexn 3
if or or gt ny 64 gt nb 512 or ne rem nb 8 0 ne rem eb 16 0
ckbad
end
if ne ckhexn 4 8
ckbad
end
nq = div nb 8
q = new ulong 64 0
for j ulong nq bound 64
put q j arw 2 j
end
o = new ulong 128 0
r = arop q nq ny o
if ne r arw 4 0
ret false
end
for j ulong div eb 16 bound 1099511627776
k = arw 3 mul j 2
if ge k 128
ckbad
end
if ne get o k arw 3 add mul j 2 1
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
